# The EKS stack's Terraform state, credentials, and provider cache still live in
# terraform/ on this branch, even though its .tf files -- and the .gitignore that
# used to sit beside them protecting these -- exist only on `main`.
#
# They have to stay on disk: terraform.tfstate is what step 0 of the runbook
# destroys the cluster with, and terraform.tfvars holds live AWS access keys.
# Without this rule a plain `git add -A` on this branch stages an access key and
# a few hundred MB of provider binaries into a public repo.
#
# Do not "clean this up" by deleting terraform/ until the decommission in
# docs/QUICK_START.md step 0 has actually been run. Losing that state file means
# hunting down every cluster resource by hand.
terraform/
